[1m[38;5;231mWhich notification data model should the design commit to?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA — derived from change log (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mAppend-only events table is the source of truth; the bell is a query plus a thin read-state table. Smallest write [39m
     [38;5;246mpath, audit log free, upgrades to C later without a rewrite.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B — materialized fan-out
     [38;5;246mOne stored notification row per recipient, written at mutation time. Simplest reads and frozen recipients, at the [39m
     [38;5;246mcost of write amplification and non-retroactive rules.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C — hybrid log + fan-out
     [38;5;246mBoth tables from day one. Right answer if you're confident email or push is coming soon and want the delivery-job [39m
     [38;5;246mshape already in place.[39m
